{
  "id": "spring-physics",
  "title": "Spring Physics Easing",
  "summary": "Spring curves as pure CSS linear() tokens, racing a plain ease-out so you can see the overshoot and settle.",
  "description": "A cubic-bezier can never leave the 0–1 range on the way out, so it can ease but never overshoot. A damped spring can. Each lane here runs the same travel through a different timing function against a dashed target line: the ease-out lane stops dead on the line, while the spring lanes sail past it and settle back. The spring curves are sampled from a damped harmonic oscillator and baked into CSS linear() tokens, so they need no JavaScript and no animation library.",
